//! run
//! panic: LYS-RT0008
//! stderr-has: '.2' does not apply to a Display type's text
//! since: 1.0.0
// §12 rule 12 (Lyric 5 12 §2 rule 5): what the compiler refuses in an f-string panics in a
// template read at run time — a spec that holds a part the value's type does not take.
import std.fmt
struct R :: Display {
    v: int
    fn show(): string = f"R{this.v}"
}
println(fmt.format("{:.2}", R { v = 1 }))
